WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.110
All right.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:05.940
Let's begin with last night's vice presidential
debate between Vice President Mike Pence and

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:11.210
Joe Biden's running mate, Kamala Harris, senator
from California.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:15.780
Expectations were very high for Kamala Harris,
her experience as a prosecutor and certainly

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:22.110
her performances during testimony in the Senate
have been parts of.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:27.050
There have been elements of why expectations
were very high for how she would do.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:28.050
And she did well.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:31.830
And I believe that she won the debate to the
extent that there was a winner.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:36.391
But I do think that she was not nearly as
tough on Mike Pence as she was on Joe Biden

00:00:36.391 --> 00:00:38.850
during Democratic primary debates.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:43.290
I think there were missed opportunities, but
I'm going to say more about that in a little

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.290
bit.

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:48.770
But the big picture here, if we want to, we
don't want to miss the forest for the trees.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:55.070
And the big picture is that Kamala Harris
did well on everything Corona virus related.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.790
She did okay on economic issues.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:02.420
And she was sort of so so on some other topics
which we will discuss.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:07.060
But if you ask me, what will the impact of
this debate be on the election, I believe

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:09.170
that it is almost zero.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:13.700
It's not zero, but it's very, very close to
zero because with everything going on with

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:18.490
Donald Trump behind in the polls, Donald Trump
releasing videos from the White House in which

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:21.920
he really doesn't look good, which we will
talk about.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.490
Nothing happened in this debate that will
change the polling very much.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:30.180
And that's not good for Donald Trump and Mike
Pence, because if you believe the polling

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:34.710
is even roughly accurate, they need something
to put them back in the lead.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:40.460
And the most likely scenario is that in the
next 72, 48, 24, in the next five minutes,

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:45.490
some new scandal will will pop up and the
vice presidential debate will be all but forgotten.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:47.390
But let's look at a few moments from it.

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:52.470
First of all, the fact that there even was
plexiglass installed at the last minute between

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.920
the candidates.

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.409
That's not good for Mike Pence.

00:01:55.409 --> 00:02:04.229
The plexiglass being needed is a topic that
in and of itself is an indictment of the Trump

00:02:04.229 --> 00:02:06.250
Penn's handling of Corona virus.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.369
And indeed, they went right into Corona virus.

00:02:09.369 --> 00:02:10.649
It was the first question.

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:15.620
I actually think this was Kamala Harris, his
best moment of the entire debate coming right

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:16.620
at the beginning.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:23.120
Well, the American people have witnessed what
is the greatest failure of any presidential

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.599
administration in the history of our country.

00:02:26.599 --> 00:02:28.870
And here are the facts.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:34.370
Two hundred and ten thousand dead people in
our country in just the last several months.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:38.090
Over seven million people who have contracted
this disease.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:41.090
One in five businesses closed.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:47.340
We're looking at frontline workers who have
been treated like sacrificial workers.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:50.240
We are looking at over 30 million people.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:55.500
Who in the last several months had to file
for unemployment.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.470
And here's the thing.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:00.209
On January twenty eighth.

00:03:00.209 --> 00:03:05.100
The vice president and the president were
informed about the nature of this pandemic.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:11.530
They were informed that it's lethal in consequence,
that it is airborne, that it will affect young

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.350
people.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:19.080
And that it would be contracted because it
is airborne.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.930
And they knew what was happening and they
didn't tell you.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.600
Can you imagine?

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:30.610
So this was Carmella's best moment if you
watched only the first question or only the

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:35.620
first 10 minutes segment, which was on Corona
virus, and then you bailed on the debate,

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:39.830
you would come away with the best possible
impression of how it went for Kamala Harris.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:45.310
The rest of the debate was more mixed because
Mike Pence kept going over his time, sometimes

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:46.849
by as much as a minute.

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:49.700
The moderator was unable to get him under
control.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:54.950
Mike Pence would continually avoid answering
the actual question being discussed by going

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:58.290
back and answering the previous question or
going to questions back.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:02.989
At one point it got so bad I wondered if Pence
was going to ask to spend some time on questions

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:05.580
from his 2016 debate with Tim Kaine.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:11.090
He just wanted to set the agenda himself and
combining that with the kind of calm, arrogant

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:13.720
delivery that Pence is known for.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:22.120
I think certainly he came up looking good
enough that his base is not going to say I

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:27.909
can no longer support Trump Pence because
of Pence, whether any undecideds were convinced

00:04:27.909 --> 00:04:31.979
to the extent that they still remain much
less clear.

00:04:31.979 --> 00:04:33.550
Here's an example of Pence doing this.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:37.259
Pence asked, Why does the U.S. have a much
higher death rate than just about every other

00:04:37.259 --> 00:04:38.259
country?

00:04:38.259 --> 00:04:43.719
Mike Pence just talks about something else
higher than that of almost every other wealthy

00:04:43.719 --> 00:04:44.719
country.

00:04:44.719 --> 00:04:46.729
And you have two minutes to respond without
interruption.

00:04:46.729 --> 00:04:48.539
And Suzanne, thank you.

00:04:48.539 --> 00:04:53.379
And I want to thank the commission and the
University of Utah for hosting this event.

00:04:53.379 --> 00:04:59.199
And Senator Harris, it's a privilege to be
on the stage with you.

00:04:59.199 --> 00:05:03.729
Our nation has gone through a very challenging
time this year.

00:05:03.729 --> 00:05:09.589
But I want the American people to know it
from the very first day President Donald Trump

00:05:09.589 --> 00:05:11.909
has put the health of America first.

00:05:11.909 --> 00:05:16.969
Before, there were more than five cases in
the United States, all people who had returned

00:05:16.969 --> 00:05:18.080
from China.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.599
So I'll spare you the torture.

00:05:19.599 --> 00:05:22.639
But he did about two minutes of that without
actually answering.

00:05:22.639 --> 00:05:27.900
Why does the United States have one of the
highest death rates per capita in the world

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.069
from Corona virus?

00:05:29.069 --> 00:05:33.360
In another moment, Mike Pence was asked about
that super spreader event that they held at

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:38.129
the White House not this past Saturday, but
the previous one, the nomination party for

00:05:38.129 --> 00:05:40.259
Amy CONI Barrett.

00:05:40.259 --> 00:05:44.669
And of course, we know that that event was
at least partially responsible for multiple

00:05:44.669 --> 00:05:49.059
instances, multiple cases of corona virus
related to the White House.

00:05:49.059 --> 00:05:50.800
Watch pens, just bail out.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:53.050
Speak up on behalf of what the American people
have done.

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:56.990
Vice President, since you were in the front
row in a Rose Garden event 11 days ago.

00:05:56.990 --> 00:06:02.009
What seems to have been a super spreader event
for senior administration congressional officials.

00:06:02.009 --> 00:06:07.259
No social distancing, few mask, and now a
cluster of corona virus cases among those

00:06:07.259 --> 00:06:08.970
who were there.

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:13.879
How can you expect Americans to follow the
administration's safety guidelines to protect

00:06:13.879 --> 00:06:18.649
themselves from Colvard when you at the White
House have not been doing so?

00:06:18.649 --> 00:06:24.979
Well, the American people have demonstrated
over the last eight months.

00:06:24.979 --> 00:06:26.430
They weren't given the facts.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:29.139
They're willing to put the health of their
families and their neighbors and people they

00:06:29.139 --> 00:06:31.860
don't even know first.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:37.379
President Trump and I have great confidence
in the American people and their ability to

00:06:37.379 --> 00:06:42.749
take that information and put it into practice
in the height of the epidemic.

00:06:42.749 --> 00:06:48.499
So that is not Penn's building to some kind
of clear answer about the super spreader event

00:06:48.499 --> 00:06:49.899
at the White House.

00:06:49.899 --> 00:06:51.909
That's Pence ranting and raving about other
things.

00:06:51.909 --> 00:06:53.249
And that was the entire debate.

00:06:53.249 --> 00:06:58.629
Here is an example of Mike Pence apparently
realizing that the corona virus portion of

00:06:58.629 --> 00:07:01.569
the debate at the beginning did not go well
for him.

00:07:01.569 --> 00:07:02.569
Here is Pence.

00:07:02.569 --> 00:07:06.409
Asked about presidential health and age and
disability.

00:07:06.409 --> 00:07:09.580
And Mike Pence just says, well, I'm going
to keep talking about Corona virus.

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:16.050
Had a conversation or reached an agreement
with President Trump about safeguards or procedures

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:19.569
when it comes to the issue of presidential
disability.

00:07:19.569 --> 00:07:21.830
And if not, do you think you should?

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.389
You have two minutes without interruption.

00:07:23.389 --> 00:07:25.349
Well, Susan, thank you.

00:07:25.349 --> 00:07:27.439
Although I would like to go back.

00:07:27.439 --> 00:07:29.300
I think we need to move on.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.300
You.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:35.899
I would like to go back because the reality
is that we're going to have a vaccine, Senator,

00:07:35.899 --> 00:07:37.159
in record time.

00:07:37.159 --> 00:07:38.300
That was the whole debate.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:40.999
I won't give you more examples of that.

00:07:40.999 --> 00:07:46.870
Mike Pence also did some of his normal theatrically,
which include refusing to accept the science

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:53.649
on climate change, repeating Donald Trump's
talking about point about how forest fires

00:07:53.649 --> 00:07:59.610
could be solved by forest management, which
they claim Democrats are either against or

00:07:59.610 --> 00:08:00.989
aren't doing.

00:08:00.989 --> 00:08:06.279
And then maybe the most bizarre moment of
the debate was when a fly landed on Mike Pence,

00:08:06.279 --> 00:08:08.809
his head, and stayed there for minutes.

00:08:08.809 --> 00:08:13.599
And the fly landing on Hypertensives Head
was funny to start with.

00:08:13.599 --> 00:08:20.139
But the fact that it seemed to be stuck and
Mike Pence's hair gel was even funnier and

00:08:20.139 --> 00:08:22.379
that instantly became a viral moment.

00:08:22.379 --> 00:08:28.029
The Joe Biden campaign immediately starting
to sell fly swatters and, you know, many,

00:08:28.029 --> 00:08:33.800
many allegories made to the biblical meaning
of when a fly lands lands on you.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:36.659
For those more religious folks in the audience,
it's it's ominous.

00:08:36.659 --> 00:08:38.229
It's not good.

00:08:38.229 --> 00:08:44.600
But the moment that many say was Kamala Harris
is worst of the debate was when the topic

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.660
of packing the courts came up.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:50.240
Now, the question came up during the Biden
Trump debate last week.

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:57.430
And the question is, if Joe Biden is elected
and Republicans confirm Amy CONI Barrett to

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:02.470
the Supreme Court, will Joe Biden pack the
Supreme Court, meaning add seats to the Supreme

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:03.560
Court?

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:07.690
And Kamala Harris, much like Joe Biden, did
not give a yes or no answer.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:11.970
And there's a lot of people who are saying
it looks really bad for Kamala not to answer

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.019
the question.

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:14.370
I'm not so sure.

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:16.270
Let let me explain.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:20.839
There clearly has been a strategic decision
made by the Biden campaign not to answer yes

00:09:20.839 --> 00:09:24.389
or no about whether Joe Biden would pack the
court.

00:09:24.389 --> 00:09:29.129
I don't think court packing is a voting issue
for many people.

00:09:29.129 --> 00:09:33.230
So really, there's a lot of potential downside
to giving a straight answer.

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:36.089
And I'll explain what I mean if they say yes
or no.

00:09:36.089 --> 00:09:42.740
They, number one, make the answer, the focus,
rather than the threat of using this in the

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:43.779
future.

00:09:43.779 --> 00:09:45.610
And if you answer yes or no.

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:48.879
The unknown threat of maybe Biden will pack.

00:09:48.879 --> 00:09:51.790
The court goes away.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:56.190
And so I understand the risk when you decide
you're not going to answer a question.

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:59.110
There's a risk that you're going to appear
evasive.

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:03.769
But I understand the strategy because I don't
think there's much to gain by saying definitively

00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:04.980
yes or no.

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:10.800
If Biden and Harris say yes, if Amy CONI Barrett
gets confirmed, we will pack the court.

00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:15.470
The right and those on the left who don't
want the court packed will go crazy.

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:20.759
And that becomes the focus rather than Republican
hypocrisy about confirming Amy CONI Barrett.

00:10:20.759 --> 00:10:26.490
With just days left before an election, if
Biden Harris say we won't pack the court,

00:10:26.490 --> 00:10:28.640
they bail out the GOP.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:32.990
And they're basically saying, even if you
confirm Amy CONI Barrett, don't worry, we're

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:34.269
not going to pack the court.

00:10:34.269 --> 00:10:39.720
So while I accept that Harris didn't answer,
I actually understand why.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:43.240
And it will be a question as to whether it
works or doesn't work.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:44.240
But that.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:45.569
But I get the strategy.

00:10:45.569 --> 00:10:50.480
Mike Pence also during the debate, seemed
to have a fat lip and his left eye was either

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:56.199
bloody with a burst blood vessel or with pinkeye,
which can sometimes happen with coronavirus.

00:10:56.199 --> 00:11:00.300
So it was impossible not to notice his physical
appearance during the debate.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:01.529
It was bizarre.

00:11:01.529 --> 00:11:04.820
But big picture, the debate was not a nothing
burger.

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:11.990
I think that you saw how you know, when Kamala
Harris went after Joe Biden in the primary,

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:16.420
you imagine there would be more ferocity and
energy from her against Mike Pence.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:19.810
And I took live calls last night after the
debate, and a bunch of my callers said, you

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:25.459
know, sometimes when women are assertive or
aggressive in popular culture, it counts against

00:11:25.459 --> 00:11:26.459
them.

00:11:26.459 --> 00:11:29.329
The Martha Stewart effect, as it's sometimes
been described.

00:11:29.329 --> 00:11:32.240
And I think that that is absolutely true to
a degree.

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:37.279
I still would have liked to see a balanced
approach that had Kamala Harris more on the

00:11:37.279 --> 00:11:39.389
offensive, which we know she can do.

00:11:39.389 --> 00:11:41.089
We've seen her do it in the Senate.

00:11:41.089 --> 00:11:43.300
We've seen her do it in other contexts.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:46.640
But the big picture is I don't think the debate
is going to change a thing.

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:51.639
And when the polling is looking so bad for
Trump and Pence, with now only 25 days left

00:11:51.639 --> 00:11:55.660
until this election, they need something to
turn it around.

00:11:55.660 --> 00:13:06.410
And this debate is not going to be the thing
that doesn't we.

